DwarfSpec Rendered Text Search Command
======================================

Purpose:
    ☐ Implement `ds.search({text="..."}, search_area?)` as a read-only query over the final rendered DFHack screen-cell buffer.
    ☐ Support borrowed native screens, ordinary mounted widgets, mounted overlays, and complete mounted screens through one public contract.
    ☐ Return the exact zero-based inclusive bounds of the selected visible text occurrence.
    ☐ Add `Subject:search(query)` as the fluent subject-scoped form of the same command.
    ☐ Keep text search spatial and render-observational; do not claim that final screen cells retain component or overlay ownership.

Completion contract:
    ☐ Complete every applicable runtime, declaration, focused-test, full-test, documentation, package, cleanup, and live-evidence item below.
    ☐ Treat this checklist as the source of truth for implementation status.
    ☐ Preserve unrelated worktree and index changes; do not stash or commit user changes.
    ☐ Record every deferred or rejected item with its rationale and the evidence that made it unnecessary or unsafe.
    ☐ Keep search read-only: do not invalidate the screen, force a render, move the pointer, send input, mutate a component, or add a named capture.
    ☐ Keep `nil` as the ordinary no-match result so `ds.search()` can be used directly as a `ds.await()` query.
    ☐ Distinguish a readable screen with no match from a region for which DFHack exposes no readable screen cells.
    ☐ Keep exact literal CP437 or byte-string matching as the initial public text model.
    ☐ Keep multiline, pattern, fuzzy, Unicode-normalized, style-aware, and render-ownership-aware search outside the initial contract.
    ☐ Distinguish focused unit, full unit, Lua syntax, package, cleanup, component-live, overlay-live, complete-screen-live, and native-live evidence in the final handoff.
    ☐ Never treat tree inspection, unit tests, package contents, or component-host rendering as proof that borrowed native-screen search works.

Locked public contract:
    ☐ Declare `dwarfspec.TextSearchQuery`.
        ☐ Require one nonempty `text` string.
        ☐ Allow `occurrence` as an optional positive integer with a default of `1`.
        ☐ Reject unknown fields.
        ☐ Match `text` literally and case-sensitively.
        ☐ Reject NUL, carriage-return, and newline bytes.
    ☐ Declare `dwarfspec.ScreenRect` as `{x1: integer, y1: integer, x2: integer, y2: integer}` using zero-based inclusive UI-grid coordinates.
    ☐ Declare `dwarfspec.TextSearchArea` as `dwarfspec.Subject|dwarfspec.ScreenRect`.
    ☐ Declare `DS.search(query, search_area?) -> dwarfspec.ScreenRect|nil`.
    ☐ Declare `Subject:search(query) -> dwarfspec.ScreenRect|nil`.
    ☐ Require a current live mount for both forms.
    ☐ Use the current mount's default search scope when `search_area` is omitted.
        ☐ Use the full current DF window for a borrowed native-screen mount.
        ☐ Use the mounted root's visible body bounds for an owned widget, overlay, or complete screen.
    ☐ Use an explicit subject's current visible body bounds as its search scope.
    ☐ Interpret an explicit rectangle in absolute UI-grid coordinates and intersect it with the current mount's default scope and current window.
    ☐ Reject stale, cleaned, foreign-mount, invisible, or unusably bounded subject areas through the existing subject-resolution and ownership contracts.
    ☐ Return occurrences in deterministic top-to-bottom, then left-to-right order.
    ☐ Return the selected occurrence's exact single-row text bounds, with `x2 = x1 + #query.text - 1` and `y2 = y1`.
    ☐ Return `nil` when the requested occurrence is absent from an otherwise readable region.
    ☐ Treat nil or unreadable cells as match-breaking sentinels.
    ☐ Fail with a stable actionable error when the entire effective region is unreadable.
    ☐ Observe the currently rendered buffer without waiting; callers that need eventual state use `ds.await()` and callers that need a new render use existing redraw or mutation commands.

Explicit exclusions:
    ☐ Do not search adapted `text` fields or aggregate component-tree text as the source of truth.
    ☐ Do not return a component, subject, widget path, render source, pen, color, tile, or capture record.
    ☐ Do not infer which component or overlay painted a matching cell.
    ☐ Do not match across row boundaries.
    ☐ Do not add Lua patterns, regular expressions, case folding, fuzzy matching, whitespace normalization, or locale behavior.
    ☐ Do not add implicit retries, timeouts, assertions, or Cypress-style query objects.
    ☐ Do not redesign `ds.get()`, `DSQuery`, selectors, or assertion chaining as part of this command.
    ☐ Do not cache screen contents until profiling shows that uncached bounded searches are inadequate.
    ☐ Do not broaden `ds.capture_screen()` or persist transient search buffers in run evidence.

